# Install-time defense against malicious lifecycle scripts in transitive
# dependencies. Local installs skip postinstall/preinstall scripts; CI's
# install-hook audit job (see .github/workflows/main.yml) catches any new
# transitive that needs a script to run, on review.
#
# First-time native-module installs (e.g. `keccak`, `secp256k1`,
# `bufferutil`) may fail to build because their postinstall didn't run.
# To override on demand:  yarn install --ignore-scripts=false
#
# See SUPPLY-CHAIN-SECURITY.md (Local install scripts policy).
--install.ignore-scripts true
